# rm — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R50 -> v1.1-A extraction -> v1.2.0 (Closes paideia-os/rm#28)
# Doc:  design/architecture.md (v1.2.0 section) in this repo;
#       design/round-retrospectives/r90-xrepo-wave3-plan.md
#         §R90-XREPO.013.M3-005 in paideia-os.
#
# Purpose
# -------
# This file is the invariant-I6 (capability handoff visible +
# refusable) manifest the shell validates at exec: rm receives
# exactly the caps below and no more. Missing a required cap in the
# reconciled set is an exec refusal; extra caps in the received set
# are dropped at cap_manifest_verify (libpdx-cap M2-001) before rm's
# main body observes them.
#
# v1.2.0 (#28) — KIND_PDXFS_VOL adoption per R90-XREPO.013.M3-005
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# R90-XREPO.013 (`design/round-retrospectives/r90-xrepo-wave3-plan.md`
# §5) shifts cap-reconciliation to EXEC TIME: shell.M2-001 invokes
# `sys_exec_reconcile_caps` for every child before returning control,
# narrowing the ambient cap-set to what the child's `caps.decl`
# declares. Every /bin coreutil (ls, cat, cp, mv, rm, mkdir, doc,
# pkg) publishes a `caps.decl` under R90-XREPO.013.M3-* so the shell
# performs the narrowing rather than granting the ambient set
# unmodified. This file is the M3-005 rm entry.
#
# The v1.2.0 rm surface is:
#
#   KIND_USER                                    -- identity root
#   KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <target-parent>)     -- default-branch unlink
#   KIND_PDXFS_FILE (rmdir, <target-parent>)     -- -r branch top-level rmdir
#   KIND_PDXFS_VOL  (unlink, <target-parent>)    -- volume-level unlink-op cap
#                                                   (declared; adoption arm
#                                                    defers to the future
#                                                    trash-move substrate)
#   KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT                            -- semantic-pipe + audit
#
# The KIND_PDXFS_VOL row is a DECLARATION and an ADOPTION NOTE rather
# than an active gate at v1.2.0. Grounds:
#
#   (1) R90-XREPO.013.M3-005 (paideia-os/rm#28) is the caps-manifest
#       half of the R90 TXN adoption plan applied to rm. Adding the
#       KIND_PDXFS_VOL row now (rather than at the future trash-move
#       landing) means the manifest reconciler will not fail-fast
#       with CAP_MANIFEST_MISSING when the trash-move body edit adds
#       the first pdxfs_txn_open call site -- the cap is already
#       declared; only the invoke happens later. The inverse ordering
#       (add-cap-when-first-called) would take two coordinated
#       releases across the InitCap sidecar packaging pipeline and
#       the loader-side reconciler.
#
#   (2) The R90 substrate has landed in-kernel (sysnos 104 / 105 /
#       107 for sys_pdxfs_txn_open / _commit / _abort per commits
#       2111 / 2112 / 2113) but the userspace side (a KIND_PDXFS_VOL
#       slot in rm's InitCap sidecar, plus the loader-side match
#       against this file) is what R90-XREPO.013.M3-005 gates.
#       Landing the declaration here without the invoke keeps that
#       gate reachable while the trash-move landing owns the body
#       edit.
#
#   (3) The manifest reconciler treats a DECLARED-but-not-INVOKED
#       cap as informational, not as CAP_MANIFEST_EXTRA. See
#       shell src/exec.pdx §exec_reconcile_publish for the ordering
#       rules; the three-arm classification (missing / extra /
#       declared) is R90-XREPO.013.M2-001 (paideia-os/shell#39).
#
# What v1.2.0 retires
# -------------------
#
# The M5-era KIND_PDXFS_TXN row (declared at rm 1.0 M1 for a future
# trash-move TXN) is DROPPED at v1.2.0: the R90 substrate uses
# KIND_PDXFS_VOL as the volume-scoping arg, not KIND_PDXFS_TXN, so
# preserving the retired row would land as CAP_MANIFEST_EXTRA at
# exec-time reconciliation. Its provenance:
#
#   KIND_PDXFS_TXN    (retired)  -- was declared at M1 for the future
#                                    trash-move TXN wrap; superseded
#                                    by the volume-scoping form the
#                                    R90 substrate uses.
#
# The elevate channel (KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL = 0x191, R48.M7 at
# paideia-os src/kernel/core/ipc/elevate_channel.pdx) is still NOT
# declared here at v1.2.0. Elevate is a per-operation request lodged
# when the resolved target is under /system/ (rm v1.2.0 #19: gate now
# runs on the sys_getcwd-resolved absolute path, not raw argv); the
# RmElevate::elevate_check_and_request call opens the channel per-op
# via libpdx-elevate, which does not require an ambient cap in rm's
# declared set. Ambient elevate authority would violate D4.
#
# Path-resolution posture (v1.2.0 #19)
# ------------------------------------
#
# The elevate gate at v1.2.0 runs on the sys_getcwd-joined absolute
# path (RmResolve::resolve_target -> sys_getcwd sysno 86 + join into
# _rm_resolved_scratch). The gate no longer sees raw argv bytes, so
# `rm ../../system/passwd` and `rm foo` (from cwd == /system) both
# fire the elevate hop correctly. Full ../ folding (a canonical
# path resolver) remains R57 substrate work; the sys_unlink kernel
# body itself walks the path via mount_root_vnode + path_resolve as
# a defence-in-depth secondary layer.
#
# Semantic-pipe emit (v1.2.0 #22)
# -------------------------------
#
# The KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT row covers both the M3-001 RemoveRecord@0.1
# schema emit via libpdx-semantic-pipe AND the M3-002 audit-broker
# send via libpdx-audit. v1.2.0 (#22) additionally fires these
# hooks from RmWalk::walk_recursive for the -r top-level target
# (previously only rm_process_one fired them). No new cap slot; the
# existing declaration covers both call sites.

requires:
  - KIND_USER
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <target-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (rmdir, <target-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_VOL  (unlink, <target-parent>)
  - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT

# Declared output schemas -- the semantic-pipe schemas rm emits on
# its stdout. RemoveRecord@0.1 fires from rm_process_one's default
# branch AND (v1.2.0 #22) from walk_recursive's -r top-level target.
declares_output_schemas:
  - RemoveRecord@0.1
